description: Clean code source structure rules for organizing code vertically, horizontally, and consistently
globs: "**/*.{php,vue,ts,js}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Clean Code: Source Structure

## Separate concepts vertically with blank lines

```php
// BAD
public function index() { return view('users.index'); }
public function store(Request $request) { ... }
private function validate(array $data) { ... }

// GOOD
public function index() { return view('users.index'); }

public function store(Request $request) { ... }

private function validate(array $data) { ... }
```

## Related code should appear vertically dense

```php
// BAD
private string $name;

private int $age;

private string $email;

// GOOD
private string $name;
private string $email;
private int $age;
```

## Declare variables close to their usage

```php
// BAD
$total = 0;
// ... 20 lines of unrelated code ...
$total = $items->sum('price');

// GOOD
$items = $this->getCartItems();
$total = $items->sum('price');
```

## Dependent functions should be close - caller above callee

```php
// GOOD
public function processOrder(Order $order): void
{
    $this->validateOrder($order);
}

private function validateOrder(Order $order): void { ... }
```

## Keep lines short (under ~120 characters)

```php
// BAD
$users = User::where('active', true)->where('role', 'admin')->where('department', 'engineering')->orderBy('created_at', 'desc')->get();

// GOOD
$users = User::query()
    ->where('active', true)
    ->where('role', 'admin')
    ->where('department', 'engineering')
    ->orderByDesc('created_at')
    ->get();
```

## Don't use horizontal alignment

```php
// BAD
$name    = 'John';
$email   = 'john@example.com';
$age     = 25;

// GOOD
$name = 'John';
$email = 'john@example.com';
$age = 25;
```

## Don't break indentation - always use braces

```php
// BAD
if ($isActive) { return true; }

// GOOD
if ($isActive) {
    return true;
}
```

## Encapsulate boundary conditions in one place

```php
// BAD - boundary logic scattered everywhere
if ($index < count($items) - 1) { ... }
if ($index <= count($items) - 1) { ... }

// GOOD
$lastIndex = count($items) - 1;
if ($index < $lastIndex) { ... }
```

## Be consistent - do similar things the same way

```typescript
// BAD - inconsistent patterns in the same codebase
const fetchUsers = async () => { ... }
function getProducts() { return axios.get(...) }

// GOOD - same pattern everywhere
const fetchUsers = async () => { ... }
const fetchProducts = async () => { ... }
```
